## Anti-patterns to Avoid

### CI/CD Anti-patterns
- ❌ **Direct production deployment**: Never deploy directly to production
- ❌ **Skipping tests**: Always run full test suite before deployment
- ❌ **Manual configuration**: Avoid manual configuration changes
- ❌ **Secrets in code**: Never commit secrets to version control
- ❌ **No rollback plan**: Always have rollback capability

### Deployment Anti-patterns
- ❌ **Blue-green without testing**: Test blue-green deployment thoroughly
- ❌ **No health checks**: Always implement proper health checks
- ❌ **Large batch deployments**: Deploy incrementally when possible
- ❌ **No monitoring**: Monitor deployments and application health
- ❌ **Ignoring security**: Security is not optional in any environment

### AWS Anti-patterns
- ❌ **Public subnets**: Use private subnets for application containers
- ❌ **Overprivileged IAM**: Follow principle of least privilege
- ❌ **No backup strategy**: Always have backup and restore procedures
- ❌ **Single AZ deployment**: Use multiple availability zones
- ❌ **No encryption**: Encrypt data in transit and at rest

